This product bundles or depends on the following third-party work.
Their licenses are unchanged by inclusion here.

Swift packages (resolved by Xcode, see backupTW.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj):

  - openac-rsa-x509-swift
    https://github.com/privacy-ethereum/openac-rsa-x509-swift
    Groth16 prover/verifier bindings for the ethereum/zkID RSA X.509 circuits.

  - Zip
    https://github.com/marmelroy/Zip
    MIT License. Used to open MyData ZIP downloads.

Rust crates (tools/official-document-physical-card-signer, DEBUG-only desktop
helper, not part of the iOS binary):

  - open-gpki-pkcs11
    https://github.com/chouhsiang/open-gpki-pkcs11
    LGPL-2.1-or-later. PKCS#11 access to the physical 自然人憑證 card.

Bundled certificates (backupTW/ZK/*.cer):

  - MOICA-G3.cer and GRCA-G3.cer are public CA certificates published by the
    Ministry of the Interior Certificate Authority (moica.nat.gov.tw) and the
    Government Root Certification Authority (grca.nat.gov.tw). Their provenance
    and SHA-256 fingerprints are recorded in backupTW/ZK/IssuerCertificate.swift.

Downloaded at runtime, pinned by SHA-256 (backupTW/ZK/CircuitAssets.swift):

  - ethereum/zkID circuit assets, release RSA-X.509-Cert-latest
    https://github.com/ethereum/zkID
  - privacy-ethereum/moica-revocation-smt revocation snapshot
    https://github.com/privacy-ethereum/moica-revocation-smt

Reference implementations studied while building the TWDIW integration
(no code copied):

  - moda-gov-tw/TWDIW-official-app (MIT)
  - denkeni, "TWDIW: The Missing Manual", https://docs.denkeni.org/twdiw
